// positive: `@copy` value composite captured by copy into a `spawn on` body
// Was a NEGATIVE while the crossing shipped the capture's box pointer, which
// put the caller's binding and the body's state on one box in two threads.
// The capture is now duplicated at its operand, so the destination's state
// holds a box of its own and the caller keeps writing to a different one.
//
// A composite carrying an arbitrary-precision value crosses too: its block has
// a non-atomic count and the duplication here RETAINS such a field, so the
// relinquishing operand un-shares every counted leaf — a duplicate for a block
// with a second holder — before the state ships (Epic 22 step 4).
@copy
type Digest = {
    value: uint64,
};

fn start(d: Digest) -> far Task<int> {
    return spawn on pool {
        ret d.value to int;
    };
}
